                        <div id="accordions" class="accordion">
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse1"><span><strong>Q1:</strong> What is a book trailer video and how does it work?</span></div></div><div id="collapse1" class="collapse show"><div class="card-body text"><p>A book trailer video is a short promotional video, typically thirty seconds to two minutes, designed to generate interest in your book the same way a film trailer generates interest in a movie. It uses visuals, music, text, and sometimes voice-over to create atmosphere and curiosity around your book without giving away the full story. Book trailers are shared on YouTube, social media, author websites, and Amazon author pages, giving potential readers a visual, emotional introduction to your book that a cover image and blurb can't replicate.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse2"><span><strong>Q2:</strong> Do you create cinematic or animated book trailers?</span></div></div><div id="collapse2" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Both. We produce cinematic trailers using live-action footage, professional colour grading, and atmospheric sound design, as well as animated trailers using motion graphics, illustrated sequences, and typographic animation. The right style depends on your genre, your budget, and where the trailer will be used. Some books suit cinematic treatment, others work better with animation, and many benefit from a combination. We'll recommend the best approach during your consultation based on your specific book and goals.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse3"><span><strong>Q3:</strong> How long does it take to produce a book trailer video?</span></div></div><div id="collapse3" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Standard production takes two to four weeks from creative brief to final delivery, depending on the complexity of the trailer and the style of production involved. Animated trailers and cinematic trailers with custom footage typically sit at the longer end. Simpler typographic or text-based trailers can be completed faster. Rush production is available for urgent launch deadlines, subject to availability. We'll give you a clear timeline during your consultation and keep you updated throughout production.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse4"><span><strong>Q4:</strong> What materials do I need to provide for a trailer?</span></div></div><div id="collapse4" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>At minimum, we need your book's cover image, a synopsis or blurb, and any specific vision you have for the trailer's tone and feel. Beyond that, the more you can share the better, key quotes from the book, comparable titles whose marketing you admire, details about your target audience, and any existing brand assets like logos or author photos. If you don't have all of this ready, that's fine. Part of our process is helping you define the creative direction during the briefing stage.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse5"><span><strong>Q5:</strong> Do you offer scriptwriting and storyboard services?</span></div></div><div id="collapse5" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, scriptwriting and storyboarding are included in our production process. We write the trailer script, including any on-screen text, narration, and visual direction, and develop a complete storyboard showing the visual sequence shot by shot before production begins. You review and approve both before anything is filmed, animated, or assembled. If you have your own script or specific text you'd like included, we're happy to work with that too.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse6"><span><strong>Q6:</strong> Is voice-over and background music included in the package?</span></div></div><div id="collapse6" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Background music is included in every trailer package, we source and license high-quality tracks that match your genre and trailer tone. Professional voice-over is available as an included or add-on element depending on your package level. We work with experienced voice-over artists across a range of styles, accents, and tonal registers, matching the narrator's voice to the feel of your book. You'll have the opportunity to approve both the voice-over artist and the music selection before they're locked into the final cut.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse7"><span><strong>Q7:</strong> Can the trailer be optimised for platforms like YouTube and social media?</span></div></div><div id="collapse7" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, platform optimisation is a core part of our delivery process. We export your trailer in every format and aspect ratio your promotional plan requires, widescreen for YouTube, vertical for Instagram Reels and TikTok, square for Facebook feeds, and any other specifications your platforms need. We also add captions for silent autoplay viewing on social media, and can produce multiple cuts at different lengths, a full trailer for YouTube, a thirty-second cut for paid advertising, a fifteen-second teaser for stories, so you have the right content for every platform without needing additional editing.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse8"><span><strong>Q8:</strong> How much does a book trailer video cost in Melbourne?</span></div></div><div id="collapse8" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Book trailer costs depend on the style of production, the length, the complexity, and how many deliverable formats are included. A typographic animation with licensed music costs less than a fully cinematic trailer with custom footage, professional voice-over, and original sound design. We don't publish fixed rates because every trailer is produced individually based on the book's requirements. Get in touch with your book details and promotional goals and we'll give you a clear, honest quote based on what your specific trailer actually needs.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse9"><span><strong>Q9:</strong> Will I be able to request revisions during production?</span></div></div><div id="collapse9" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, revisions are built into every stage of our process. You review and approve the script and storyboard before production begins, then review the first assembled cut with the opportunity to request changes to pacing, text, music, colour, and any other element. We revise until you're happy with the final product. Our goal is a trailer you're genuinely proud to share, so we don't rush approvals or treat revision requests as inconveniences.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse10"><span><strong>Q10:</strong> Can the trailer be customised according to my book's genre and audience?</span></div></div><div id="collapse10" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Absolutely, customisation isn't an optional extra, it's the entire point. A thriller trailer needs tension and pace. A romance trailer needs warmth and emotional pull. A business book trailer needs clean authority. A children's book trailer needs energy and charm. Every trailer we produce is built from scratch around your specific genre, your target audience, and the emotional response you want the viewer to walk away with. We don't apply the same visual template across different categories and hope it works. The genre shapes every creative decision from the first frame to the last.</p></div></div></div>
